    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "NEW YORK CITY\nDONG KINGMAN",
      "Cocktailo\nSherry Dubonnet Campari\nManhattan Gin Martini Vodka Martini Vermouth\nBloody Mary Screwdriver Whiskey Sour\nTom Collins Vodka Collins Daiquiri\nScotch Bourbon\nCanadian Gin Vodka Rum\nPremium Beer\nMenus\nAperitivo\nApéritif\nDelicias Culinarias\nSeleção de Hors d'Oeuvre\nSelected Gourmet Delicacies\nFilete de Lomo, Maître d'Hôte\nBife de Lombo Grelhado\nGrilled Tenderloin Steak\nGuiso de Cordero, Salsa Curry\nCaril de Carneiro, Molho Curry\nLamb Curry\nPato a la Naranja\nPato à California\nDuck à l'Orange\nPapas a la Casera\nBatatas à Moda da Casa\nPotatoes Maison",
      "Café\nCafé\nCoffee\nVIIY\nCaril de Carneiro, Molho Cury\nLamb Curry\nPato a la Naranja\nPato à California\nDuck à l'Orange\nPapas a la Casera\nBatatas à Moda da Casa\nPotatoes Maison\nArroz Pilaf\nRice Pilaf\nLegumbres en Mantequilla\nLegumes na Manteiga\nButtered Vegetable Bouquet\nEnsalada Mixta\nSalada Campinha\nTossed Garden Salad\nSelección de Frutas y Quesos\nVariedade de Queijos e Frutas Frescas\nSelected Fruits and Cheeses\nPostre\nSobremesa\nDessert\nCafé Descafeinado\nCafé sem Cafeina\nDecaffeinated Coffee\nSelected Red and White Wines\nChampagne Brut\nDrambuie Bénédictine Crème de Menthe\nCognac Napoléon Cointreau\nKahlua\nAmaretto di Saronno\n215 KP$572",
      "NEW YORK CITY\nDong Kingman, the award winning Chinese-American artist, travels the world sketching and painting\nthe beautiful, the monumental and the picturesque. His watercolors grace more than forty\npermanent museum and private collections in the USA and abroad\nOne of the most remarkable real estate deals in history was negotiated in 1624 when Peter Minuit\nbought the island of Manhattan from the Indians for a reported $24 worth of trinkets.\nToday, a city of almost 8 million people, New York is perhaps the greatest port in the world and the\nfinancial, intellectual and artistic center of the United States of America. It is a city of superlatives,\nin a class by itself. Pan Am serves New York every day on its Round-the-World flights, and one\ncan reach New York on Pan Am from virtually anywhere in the world.\nPAN AM.\n200|.080.238"
    ],
